{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>For it had not been specified what should be done to him.</b> By which form of death he would die; but they did know that 'he who profanes it shall surely be put to death' — ״מחלליה מות יומת״. And HaShem, exalted be He, specified and said: ״מות יומת האיש רגום אותו באבנים״ — 'the man shall surely be put to death; you shall stone him with stones' — that is to say, 'shall surely be put to death' (מות יומת), which is written in ״מחלליה מות יומת,״ means stoning (סקילה)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:45.966629831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}